First Author: Kampaktsis
Title: Machine learning-based prediction of mortality after heart transplantation in adults with congenital heart disease: A UNOS database analysis
Source number: 25  ￼

Very short summary: This retrospective UNOS study developed and internally validated a CatBoost machine-learning model to predict mortality after heart transplantation in adults with congenital heart disease (ACHD). Five key findings were: (1) the cohort included 1033 ACHD recipients undergoing isolated heart transplantation; (2) 1-year mortality was 19.9% with 205 deaths; (3) 10 variables were selected from 49 candidates for the final 1-year model; (4) the 1-year model achieved AUC 0.80, accuracy 75.2%, sensitivity 75%, specificity 75%, PPV 42%, and NPV 93%; and (5) SHAP identified post-transplant hemodialysis, eGFR, ischemic time, age, and total bilirubin as the most influential predictors. Figures 1–5 and the reported tables were used directly for this extraction.  ￼

